  <h2 id="chennai">Why the shift to M-Sand matters in Chennai</h2>
  <p>Chennai's construction boom from 2015 onwards, combined with successive court orders restricting Palar and Cauvery river sand mining, has forced a market shift to M-Sand. The Tamil Nadu government now officially recognises M-Sand as an equivalent of river sand for most applications. Building codes, structural engineers, and ready-mix concrete plants have all adapted.</p>
  <p>The result: M-Sand in Chennai today is reliable, certified, and cheaper. River sand is a specialty, premium-priced, and harder to source. New homeowners almost never need to think about river sand — and that's a good thing.</p>

  <h2 id="check">How to check M-Sand quality on delivery</h2>
  <p>Five field tests you can run in under two minutes when the tipper arrives. Full details in our <a href="/guides/quality-check">M-Sand quality check guide</a>. In short: silt test in a water bottle, palm test for grit, particle shape inspection, gradation mix, and ask for the IS 383 mill sheet.</p>

  <h2 id="price">How price compares in 2026</h2>
  <p>As of June 2026, OneInfra's M-Sand prices are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Washed M-Sand:</strong> ₹ 1,250/ton (≈ ₹ 1,750 per unit)</li>
    <li><strong>Double-washed P-Sand:</strong> ₹ 1,400/ton (≈ ₹ 2,000 per unit)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>River sand, when available, runs ₹ 1,500-1,800/ton — but with frequent stockouts. For a typical 1,000 sq ft home, switching to M-Sand saves ₹ 5,000-8,000 on materials alone, with no quality compromise.</p>

  <h2 id="call">When to call us</h2>
  <p>If you have an architect's BOQ and want us to quote against it, call <a href={`tel:${site.phoneTel}`}>{site.phone}</a> or WhatsApp the quantities. If you just want to know which grade of M-Sand to use for your specific job, ask on the call — we'll tell you in plain English without upselling.</p>

  <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: var(--space-8); padding: var(--space-4); border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md);">
    <strong>OneInfra position:</strong> we only stock washed, IS 383 graded M-Sand and P-Sand. We do not stock unwashed crusher dust under the M-Sand label, and we will tell you if a different material would suit your job better.
  </p>
